2026-11-24 | (intake commit, see git log for vendor/basicpitch) | INITIAL INTAKE @e0cf072d59fc87846e5be6ee7841bf726552ce9b: vendored LICENSE (MIT, © 2024 Sevag H, byte-identical, sha256 a098fd72…24aa9) + src/basicpitch.hpp + src/midi_notes.cpp + src/ort_inference.cpp. NOT vendored: src_cli/, src_wasm/, web/, scripts/, ort-model/* (the weights and the ort-builder artifacts — weights never enter git, AGENTS §6), and every submodule (vendor/onnxruntime, vendor/libremidi, vendor/libnyquist, vendor/oboe-resampler, vendor/ort-builder, vendor/eigen — Eigen is REUSED from vendor/demucs.cpp/third_party/eigen, same pin, D-32.5). Ruling: D-39. Compile smoke: g++ 13.3.0 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -fsyntax-only against the real vendored Eigen + a throwaway minimal ORT C++ API stub in /tmp (NOT committed): both sources compile; one PRE-EXISTING upstream warning (unused 'max_energy' in apply_melodia_trick). The real ORT compile proof is P-301's basicpitch-spike job (L-302).
2026-11-24 | (intake commit) | PATCH 1 — src/midi_notes.cpp: removed `#include <libremidi/libremidi.hpp>` and `#include <libremidi/writer.hpp>`. WHY (D-39 §3): libremidi is not needed (we emit NoteTrack JSON / UltraStar text, not MIDI files) and its own license reads NOASSERTION on GitHub — unknown license = not shipped (AGENTS §9). Side effect: the file no longer references libremidi at all (asserted by the patch script).
2026-11-24 | (intake commit) | PATCH 2 — src/midi_notes.cpp: deleted the static helper `model_frames_to_time()` and everything from `static uint32_t time_to_ticks(...)` to end-of-file (i.e. `time_to_ticks`, `note_events_to_midi`, `basic_pitch::convert_to_midi`). WHY (D-39 §3): the whole MIDI-writing tail depends on libremidi; `model_frames_to_time` was used only by that tail (grep-verified: one call site, inside `note_events_to_midi`), so keeping it would leave an unused static function. The note-event extraction (`find_peaks`, `apply_melodia_trick`, `add_pitch_bends`, `drop_overlapping_pitch_bends`, `output_to_notes_polyphonic`) is untouched.
2026-11-24 | (intake commit) | PATCH 3 — src/midi_notes.cpp + src/basicpitch.hpp: `output_to_notes_polyphonic` is now EXPORTED (dropped `static`; declared in the header) and replaces the removed `convert_to_midi` declaration. WHY (D-39 §3): upstream exposed only `convert_to_midi` (a MIDI byte blob) — our bridge needs the note events themselves. Header also documents that `NoteEvent.start_idx`/`end_idx` are FRAME indices at ANNOTATIONS_FPS (22050/256 ≈ 86.13 Hz) and `pitch` is already MIDI (`freq_idx + MIDI_OFFSET`).
2026-11-24 | (intake commit) | PATCH 4 — src/ort_inference.cpp + src/basicpitch.hpp: the model is loaded from a FILE PATH instead of the baked-in `model.ort` blob — removed `#include "model.ort.h"`, changed the session to `Ort::Session session(env, model_path.c_str(), session_options)`, and threaded a `const std::string &model_path` parameter through both `ort_inference()` overloads. WHY (D-39 §1 + §6 + AGENTS §6): (a) one ORT runtime — the EXISTING SPM ONNX Runtime 1.24.2 (D-13), not ort-builder's trimmed ORT (rejected: duplicate ORT symbols / static-link hazard / version skew); (b) the weights live in the app's model cache, downloaded once and SHA256-verified — they are never committed to git; (c) the upstream baked-in form is a 1.84 MB C source file that we refuse to vendor. The session input/output names ("serving_default_input_2:0", "StatefulPartitionedCall:0/1/2") are unchanged and match the .onnx export.
